SETUP / GETTING STARTED
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Target network : Morph Hoodi Testnet
Chain ID       : 2910
RPC            : https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
Explorer       : https://explorer-hoodi.morphl2.io
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Prerequisites
  - Foundry  (forge, cast)   https://getfoundry.sh
  - Node.js 18+
  - pnpm
  - A wallet with Hoodi ETH for gas
    Faucet: https://morphl2.io/faucet  (select Hoodi testnet)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 — Build the contracts
  cd packages/contracts
  forge build
Output ABIs land in packages/contracts/out/
The backend imports them from there — do not skip this step.
Also run forge build after any contract changes.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 — Deploy MockUSDC on Morph Hoodi
MockUSDC has a built-in faucet — no initial mint needed at deploy time.
Users call mint() directly or use POST /faucet/mint after deployment.
  forge script script/DeployMockUSDC.s.sol \
    --rpc-url morph_hoodi \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --broadcast
Copy the printed MockUSDC address.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3 — Deploy APIRegistry + X402Facilitator on Morph Hoodi
Use the MockUSDC address from step 2.
TREASURY_ADDRESS is the wallet that collects the 1% platform fee.
  USDC_ADDRESS=<MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
  TREASURY_ADDRESS=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS> \
  forge script script/Deploy.s.sol \
    --rpc-url morph_hoodi \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --broadcast
Copy the printed APIRegistry and X402Facilitator addresses.
Verify on explorer: https://explorer-hoodi.morphl2.io
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 4 — Configure the backend .env
Edit apps/backend/.env:
  RPC_URL=https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
  CHAIN_NAME=morph_hoodi
  GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY=<YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY>
  API_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=<APIREGISTRY_ADDRESS>
  X402_FACILITATOR_ADDRESS=<X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS>
  USDC_ADDRESS=<MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS>
  PROVIDER_ADDRESS=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS>
  TREASURY_ADDRESS=<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS>
  FACILITATOR_DEPLOY_BLOCK=<BLOCK_NUMBER_FROM_DEPLOYMENT_RECEIPT>
GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY       — backend wallet that calls facilitator.settle() on-chain
PROVIDER_ADDRESS          — wallet that receives 99% of each API payment
TREASURY_ADDRESS          — wallet that receives the 1% platform fee
FACILITATOR_DEPLOY_BLOCK  — block number when X402Facilitator was deployed
                            (avoids scanning from block 0 on startup)
                            Find it in the forge script broadcast output
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 5 — Install backend dependencies
  cd apps/backend
  pnpm install
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 6 — Start the backend
  pnpm dev
Server starts on http://localhost:3001
  GET  /config                      public config (contract addresses, quickstart)
  GET  /                            health check
  PAID APIs (require X-Payment header)
  GET  /api/v1/catalog              list all APIs with prices
  GET  /api/v1/btc                  BTC/USD price  ($0.001 USDC)
  GET  /api/v1/eth                  ETH/USD price  ($0.001 USDC)
  GET  /api/v1/sol                  SOL/USD price  ($0.0005 USDC)
  GET  /api/v1/gas                  Gas tracker    ($0.0005 USDC)
  GET  /api/v1/call/:apiId          proxy any registered API (dynamic price)
  REGISTRY
  GET  /registry/apis               list all registered APIs
  GET  /registry/api/:id            single API detail + activity
  GET  /registry/provider/:address  APIs by provider
  GET  /registry/stats              total count + chain status
  POST /registry/register           register a new API on-chain
  PUT  /registry/api/:id            update price or active status
  PAYMENT
  GET  /payment/nonce               get fresh nonce + deadline (5 min)
  POST /payment/verify              pre-flight signature check
  GET  /payment/balance/:address    USDC balance
  GET  /payment/status              payment layer health
  FAUCET (testnet only)
  GET  /faucet/status/:address      check eligibility and cooldown
  POST /faucet/mint                 mint 1000 MockUSDC to a wallet
  DASHBOARD
  GET  /dashboard/:address          wallet overview (spend, history)
  GET  /dashboard/:address/history  paginated call history
  GET  /dashboard/:address/spend    spend breakdown per API
  PROVIDER PORTAL
  GET  /provider/:address           provider overview (earnings, APIs)
  GET  /provider/:address/earnings  earnings breakdown per API
  GET  /provider/:address/calls     incoming call history
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 7 — Get MockUSDC (agent/user onboarding)
Option A — via backend faucet:
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/faucet/mint \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"address": "<YOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS>"}'
Option B — call mint() directly on-chain:
  cast send <MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
    "mint()" \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
Each wallet can mint 1000 USDC once per hour (enforced by the contract).
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 8 — Approve USDC spending (agent wallet)
The agent wallet must approve the X402Facilitator to pull USDC.
This is a one-time on-chain transaction per agent wallet.
  cast send <MOCK_USDC_ADDRESS> \
    "approve(address,uint256)" \
    <X402FACILITATOR_ADDRESS> \
    115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007913129639935 \
    --private-key <AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
Note: The Gemini agent (agent/index.mjs) handles mint + approve automatically.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 9 — Make a paid API call (test script)
  - node apps/backend/scripts/pay.mjs
The script does everything autonomously:
  1. Fetches nonce + deadline from GET /payment/nonce
  2. Signs the payment message with GATEWAY_PRIVATE_KEY
  3. Pre-flight verifies via POST /payment/verify
  4. Calls GET /api/v1/btc with a single X-Payment header (base64 JSON)
  5. Prints the HTTP status and BTC price response
X-Payment header format:
  base64(JSON({ payer, provider, amount, nonce, deadline, signature }))
On success the gateway settles on Morph Hoodi via
X402Facilitator.settle(payer, provider, ...) — no human approval needed.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 10 — Run the Gemini AI agent (optional)
  cd agent
  npm install
  cp .env.example .env
  # Fill in GEMINI_API_KEY and AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY
  node index.mjs "Analyze the crypto market and give a trading recommendation"
The agent:
  - Auto-mints MockUSDC if balance is 0
  - Auto-approves the facilitator if allowance is 0
  - Reads the catalog and gives Gemini the tools
  - Gemini decides which APIs to call
  - Agent pays for each call autonomously via x402
  - Gemini synthesizes a final analysis
----------------------------------------------------------------------
How the autonomous payment flow works
  Agent                Gateway (backend)           Morph Hoodi
    │                        │                          │
    │── GET /api/v1/btc ────▶│                          │
    │◀── 402 Payment Req ────│                          │
    │    (amount, facilitator│                          │
    │     chainId, nonce URL)│                          │
    │                        │                          │
    │── GET /payment/nonce ─▶│                          │
    │◀── { nonce, deadline } │                          │
    │                        │                          │
    │  [signs off-chain]     │                          │
    │                        │                          │
    │── GET /api/v1/btc ────▶│                          │
    │   X-Payment: base64(   │── verifyPayment()        │
    │   {payer,provider,     │   (ECDSA off-chain)      │
    │    amount,nonce,sig})  │                          │
    │◀── 200 OK + data ──────│                          │
    │                        │── facilitator.settle() ─▶│
    │                        │   (payer, provider, sig) │
    │                        │                          │── verify sig == payer
    │                        │                          │── transferFrom(payer→provider)
    │                        │                          │── emit PaymentSettled
    │                        │◀── txHash ────────────── │
